- label: the unified live chat works for opencode's virtual sessions, not only file-backed recordings: sessionFreshnessPath maps an opencode:// path to the resolved opencode.db file so /api/sessions/live's etag stat and liveSessionActivity's memo stat both track the growing database instead of 404ing on a virtual path, GET /api/sessions/live?id=opencode://<id> answers the full parsed session with source opencode, and new rows appended to the db surface through the normal etag flow
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'opencode live|opencode session' test/routes/session-live-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, api, implemented]
- label: origin-agnostic liveness is proven in a real served browser across MULTIPLE non-claude sources at once: with stub agent processes (script stubs whose argv matches the per-binary pgrep patterns) running in the fixture cwds of a cursor, a factory, and an opencode session simultaneously, the dashboard renders one external RUNNING row per source with the full unified anatomy (running badge, source pill, project chip, prompt), the overview running counter equals the number of live agents, and a non-claude row's click target opens the honest watch-only live chat for that session
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/unified-live-chat.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, tests, browser-live, implemented]
# unified-live
- label: GET /api/sessions/live?id=<hash|path>[&etag=…] (registered in ROUTE_MAP, never route-cached) is the session-keyed live parsed-session endpoint — the /api/runs/session machinery (etag-memoized incremental parse via the shared per-path memo, one stat per poll while idle, {unchanged:true} on a repeated etag) generalized to ANY session regardless of origin; it answers {sessionHash, sessionPath, source, project, live, state, run, etag, session, chapters} where live comes from detectLiveSessions, state is the generating word "running"|"idle" (running iff live; idle is not an error — the transcript stays served and liveness can return), run is {id, status} when the recording belongs to a tracequest run (resolved read-only, never persisting a link; status is the same generating word running|idle|exited) else null, and the parse receives the session's discovered source so non-claude recordings parse correctly; the endpoint is read-only (no Host guard per the read-endpoint posture) and the id follows resolveSessionPathForRequest semantics exactly — 400 missing, 403 non-session path (never touching the filesystem), 404 unknown hash, 409 ambiguous — so paths outside the agent session roots can never resolve, and a recording vanishing answers 404 JSON
  id: ulep
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/routes/session-live-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, api, implemented]
- label: GET /run?session=<hash|path> serves the read-only watch page for a session tracequest did not launch — src/browser/run-page.js liveSessionPage, sharing the CHAT_TRANSCRIPT_JS chunk with runPage so the transcript treatment (user bubbles, markdown-lite prose, thought markers, tool cards, Explored grouping, sticky scroll, etag-gated re-render) is byte-identical to a run's chat; the client polls /api/sessions/live at the run cadence (SESSION_POLL_MS) with the etag flow, liveness lapsing flips the page to an honest idle state (gray dot, "Not running" marker) WITHOUT stopping the poll loop (an idle agent can resume — only a 404 stops it via the gone state), and the handle shares resolveSessionPathForRequest semantics answered as the run-style error page (400/403/404 with a "session watch" kicker, never "live session watch"); the page title and observer heading use running|idle (never live session); ?id wins over ?session so run links stay unambiguous
  id: ulpg
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'unified-live|live-session watch|session mode' test/browser/run-page.test.js test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, ui, implemented]
- label: the live-session watch page replaces the composer with an HONEST read-only state — no input box, no send button, no stop/kill controls, no /api/runs/input wiring, and no raw-terminal block (there is no tmux pane to capture); instead the status strip carries the pulsing dot + "Running — driven outside tracequest" (idle variant when liveness lapses) with a right-aligned watch-only chip, the header carries a muted "external" origin chip and an always-visible "view session" cross-link, and an observer card states exactly what this is ("started outside tracequest … no composer here … to steer it, use the terminal where it is running") and what IS possible: Open full session view, Export markdown, and — when the recording turns out to be some run's — an accented "Open run chat <runId>" link into the steerable chat
  id: ulro
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'honest read-only|identical transcript|header and identity' test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, ui, implemented]
- label: the dashboard speaks ONE status vocabulary AND one anatomy for live agents — launched runs and external live sessions both render through the SINGLE shared row builder liveAgentRowHtml (browser-client.js), so origin can never fork the card: identical run-row chrome, run-state-badge "running", source pill, id, model, project, prompt, the server-derived activity line with the same pulsing dot (honest "Working…" fallback while live), grade chip via the same computeGrade path, and the full stat row; external rows differ ONLY as data — a muted "external" origin chip (title-text explains it honestly) and the absence of genuinely impossible controls (no kill/dismiss: there is no run window to kill) — and the bundle now defines sumToolCounts/includesLower so client-side grading of uncached live rows can never throw; render() pins external live rows next to run rows on page 1 and absorbs their plain session rows (pinnedLivePaths) so every live agent is ONE object with ONE click target — the live chat (/run?id=@N for runs, /run?session=<hash> for external) — the separate Live strip stays deleted and the list-row live indicator badge reads "running"
  id: uldb
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/browser-client.test.js test/browser/browser-page-build.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, ui, implemented]
- label: /view of an external live session injects the same floating cross-link chip a run recording gets — "running session · open chat" with data-status=running targeting /run?session=<hash> (liveWatchChipFor, rendered only when the run chip did not fire and detection still reports the path live), so the full session page and the live chat cross-link both ways for any origin
  id: ulvw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'live watch chip' test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, ui, implemented]
- label: the unified live chat is proven in a real served browser — an externally-simulated live session (a codex-format session file held open by the test process, the open-fd liveness path, while being appended) opens at /run?session=<hash> with the transcript rendered (user bubble + assistant prose), the read-only state visible (watch-only chip, observer note, no input box or send button, "driven outside tracequest" status), appended events rendering without a reload while chat polling stays active, and the dashboard's unified live row navigating straight into that chat view on click; and with BOTH origins live at once (a stub-claude run launched through POST /api/runs in a private tmux + the fd-held codex session) the overview running counter reads 2, both cards carry the identical anatomy (running badge, source/id/project chips, prompt, in-progress "Running <command>" activity line with pulsing dot, stat row), and each card click lands in its own live chat
  id: ulpw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/unified-live-chat.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, tests, browser-live, implemented]
- label: every live counter derives from ONE origin-agnostic is-live definition — liveNow() (shared app-chrome source, embedded in browser-client.js and run-page.js) counts generating launched runs (runIsLive: never tmux status running alone) plus externally detected live sessions with s.live === true, deduped by recording path so a run and its own recording never double-count (exited and idle-launched runs never count); the dashboard Overview "running" stat renders liveNow(), never _liveSessions.length alone; the run-page shell rail paints #appLive and its overview running stat from liveNow() too, never a filtered or run-absorbed loop or a hardcoded running status
  id: ulcn
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'liveNow|LIVE counter|rail rows carry the live activity|D1' test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, ui, implemented]
- label: every detected live session carries the SAME server-derived activity line a run row gets — liveSessionActivity (route-handlers-launch.js) reuses runActivityLine through the shared etag-keyed parse memo, the session's discovered source picks the parser, and any failure degrades to null exactly like a run's line; /api/sessions (handleApiSessions) and the initial dashboard embed (browserPage) annotate liveSessions[].activity with it, and the run-page rail's external rows lead with that line (origin stays an honest " · external" suffix) — the derivation exists once, origin-agnostic, never twice
  id: ulsa
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'liveSessionActivity|origin-agnostic activity' test/routes/launch-routes.test.js test/routes/route-handlers-api-cache.test.js
  tags: [spec, unified-live, api, implemented]
